---
config:
  flowchart:
    nodeSpacing: 24
    wrappingWidth: 240
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the end-to-end tests run
    accDescr: run.sh drives a Docker Compose project. It talks to Nextcloud, which runs this checkout as a custom app, through occ, WebDAV and the routes of the app; it sets the scenario and the tasks of the Paperless mock, mock_server.py, which Nextcloud calls through the REST API; and it starts Chromium in the image of Playwright, which runs accessibility.mjs, keyboard.mjs, settings.mjs, files.mjs, flow.mjs and screenshots.mjs against Nextcloud. On request, Nextcloud keeps its tables in MariaDB or PostgreSQL instead of SQLite, and its files in an object store with the API of S3.

    run["run.sh"]
    subgraph compose ["Docker Compose project"]
        browser["Chromium in<br>the image of<br>Playwright:<br>accessibility.mjs,<br>keyboard.mjs,<br>settings.mjs,<br>files.mjs,<br>flow.mjs,<br>screenshots.mjs"]
        nextcloud["Nextcloud<br>this checkout<br>as a custom app"]
        mock["Paperless mock<br>mock_server.py"]
        database[("MariaDB or<br>PostgreSQL")]
        s3[("SeaweedFS:<br>an object store<br>with the API<br>of S3")]
    end

    run --> browser
    run -- "occ, WebDAV,<br>the routes<br>of the app" --> nextcloud
    run -- "scenario,<br>tasks" --> mock
    browser --> nextcloud
    nextcloud -- "REST API" --> mock
    nextcloud -. "tables" .-> database
    nextcloud -. "files" .-> s3

    classDef nextcloud fill:#0082c92e,stroke:#0082c9,stroke-width:2px
    classDef paperless fill:#17803d2e,stroke:#17803d,stroke-width:2px
    classDef data fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class nextcloud nextcloud
    class mock paperless
    class database,s3 data
